38:24.185 --> 38:36.476
[SPEAKER_01]: describe and to test because each and every one of us has different body configuration. Some have longer torso and maybe larger bellies, I

38:36.796 --> 38:48.422
[SPEAKER_01]: don't know, the larger shoulders. So this is very difficult to assess testing for one harness. I personally find that harnesses are very

38:48.462 --> 39:00.168
[SPEAKER_01]: different from they used to be because at the time there were harnesses with cross-bracing and long ago there were harnesses with nothing. No

39:00.228 --> 39:11.574
[SPEAKER_01]: IBS, no cross-bracing, low attachment points, very weight- shifty. And the evolution of those harnesses came along to make that balance

39:12.374 --> 39:23.716
[SPEAKER_01]: between harnesses weight shifting, and stability. A bit more stable, I think. Yeah, I think I found Harris today a bit more stable than that used

39:23.736 --> 39:39.735
[SPEAKER_01]: to be. But also, if manufacturers want to sell gliders to lots of pilots, they have to find solution for the majority. And the majority I like

39:40.436 --> 39:51.041
[SPEAKER_01]: glider that is easy, stable, so I have to make a stable harness and have to make stable gliders. And the harnesses of today are very different from

39:51.101 --> 40:00.787
[SPEAKER_01]: the gliders and the harnesses of yesterday. It's totally different, like you're flying in one wheel cycle and now you're flying with four

40:00.807 --> 40:11.638
[SPEAKER_01]: wheel cycle. I personally prefer a seat board harness. because seat board harness can put your pressure on your hips to weight shift

40:12.359 --> 40:23.745
[SPEAKER_01]: precisely into the turn. That's the best way to do it. Seatless harnesses probably are comfortable, but seatless harnesses are a bit

40:23.785 --> 40:34.649
[SPEAKER_01]: difficult to assess the weight shift on your hips. You won't have a pressure point. You feel lost. If I get a big collapse on a seatless

40:34.689 --> 40:46.290
[SPEAKER_01]: harness, I find that my torso is just facing down quickly. You don't have a point. or you have to hold on the risers, and that's not good. That's

40:46.370 --> 40:55.576
[SPEAKER_01]: about harnesses. Do you have any thoughts about the fairings? Because some manufacturers come out with no fairing, then some have pretty long

40:55.696 --> 41:03.601
[SPEAKER_00]: ones, and then now we are, of course, seeing the cocoon ones. The fairing, of course, is nice to have. It looks good for competitions.

41:04.329 --> 41:16.298
